  "miniwob_commit": "33c3b4ddef8c6eb67c57a29663d844b1eda7e614",
  "regrouped": "The 18 pointer-marked tasks are their own group from 01b43b1 on. Read this as what it is: c8ed86e's committed rule said they 'stay in the click group, which depresses its success rather than inflating it', 28816 ran on that 72-task group, and the decision to read the 18 apart was made after its first 28 episodes -- which failed on bisect-angle and circle-center, two of them. Naming them in advance is not the same as pre-registering the decision to analyse them separately, and claiming otherwise was the self-serving version. So 28816's primary result is the verdict over the whole 72, the 54/18 split is secondary and dated after that data, and runs from 01b43b1 cannot be combined with 28816 at all because the fast mode's action set changed (scroll). code-reviewer required this reading.",
  "rule": "beyond click when the page has a text field or a <select>; pointer-only tasks are not detected and stay in the click group, which depresses its success rather than inflating it",
